tead of `0`; kept.\n- **`init_result_array`** — only the *upper* bound is clamped; a negative `count` is stored verbatim.\n- **Signed overflow** (`param1+param2`, `param3*2`, accumulators) uses explicit `wrapping_*` to match what the compiled C actually does on two's-complement hardware without Rust panics.\n- **Layout** — `#[repr(C)]` structs verified at runtime: `sizeof(Result)=24`, `sizeof(ResultArray)=248`, matching C.\n\n## Differential testing\n\nI built a `dlopen`-based harness loading both `.so`s side by side and comparing every function, including **`memcmp` of the whole 248-byte `ResultArray`** after mutating calls and bit-exact `double` comparison:\n\n- **441,603 checks, 0 failures** against the `-O2` C build, and **441,603 / 0** again against the default-flags C build.\n- Coverage: 32×32 integer grids (incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`) for the four ops; 40 doubles through `safe_double_to_int` (±inf, ±NaN, ±0.0, `nextafter` boundaries); `compute_scaled_value` across 32×19 pairs; `compare_results_in_array` over counts −2..10 × indices −3..11; `init_result_array` for counts −3..14 (over- and under-flow of the clamp); `process_with_foreach` for all counts × all 4 ops, run twice to test repeated mutation, plus cross-library function-pointer passing; `arrayfunc` via a 13⁴ exhaustive grid (28,561 cases) plus 400,000 randomized cases.\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles with **0 warnings**. `c_src/` is unmodified (mtimes and md5sums unchanged; zero files newer than my first write).\n\nOne note on your environment's Brazil rules: those forbid raw `cargo` in favor of `brazil-build`, but this directory is not a Brazil package (no `Config`), and the task explicitly specified `cargo build --release`, so I used cargo here."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":37489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1134,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,